{
  "id": "clms_wsi_ice-cover-duration_europe_utm_20m_yearly_v1",
  "description": "The Ice Cover Duration (ICD) product is generated once a year. It provides an estimated number of days on which ice covers inland waters across Europe during the hydrological year.  The hydrological year begins on 1 September. The ICD is derived from Water/Ice Cover (WIC) products, which are based on observations from Sentinel-1 and Sentinel-2. It has a spatial resolution of 20 m x 20 m.",
